<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3215] &apos;pid&apos; files cannot be deleted when interpreter is restarted.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3215</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When user click &apos;restart interpreter&apos;, pid file about interpreter can be remained.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But it can be removed when zeppelin is shutting down so it is not critical bug of zeppelin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But zeppelin&apos;s shutdown process can kill another process if OS reuse pid that is used interpreter because &apos;zeppelin-daemon.sh&apos; kill process with run/*.pid files.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
